    "note": [
     {
      "text": "51-year-old female presenting with excessive thirst and frequent urination for 5 weeks. Character: passing urine many times, also at night; radiation: n/a; aggravated by sweet food; relieved by nothing. Severity 3/10. Associated: tiredness. PMH: Type 2 diabetes for 8 years; Appendectomy in 2001. Drugs: Metformin 500 mg. Allergy: no known allergies. Family: no similar illness. Personal: non-smoker, no alcohol. Triage: ROUTINE."
